# Tests

## Every feature and every fix comes with tests

Every `feature/`, `bugfix/` and `hotfix/` branch that changes code contains the matching
tests in the **same branch**. No tests, no merge.

| Change                          | Required tests |
|---------------------------------|----------------|
| New feature / new API           | Unit tests for the new behaviour incl. edge and error cases |
| Bugfix / hotfix                 | Regression test that **fails without the fix** and passes with it |
| Math / geometry                 | known values **and** invariants (see below) |
| Renderer / visible output       | jsdom/mock test of the output **plus** a browser check (Playwright or Chrome DevTools): compare Canvas and SVG, look at a screenshot |
| Public API / README             | update `test/readme.test.ts` or `test/dist/verify-dist.mjs` |
| Refactoring without behaviour change | existing tests stay green unchanged; add missing coverage first |

Exception: docs/rules/CI-only changes without code – there, only keep `npm run check` green.

Fixing bugs: write the failing test first and see it red, then fix.
Name the added tests in the merge/commit text and in the answer to the user.

## Conventions

- **All tests live in `test/`** – never in `src/`, `demo/` or anywhere else.
  The structure mirrors `src/`: `src/math/Mat4.ts` → `test/math/Mat4.test.ts`,
  `src/renderers/SVGRenderer.ts` → `test/renderers/svg.test.ts`.
  `test/structure.test.ts` fails as soon as a test file is outside `test/`;
  Vitest only runs `test/**/*.test.ts` anyway.
- Shared helpers in `test/helpers.ts`, bundle smoke test in `test/dist/verify-dist.mjs`,
  README examples in `test/readme.test.ts`. Always import code via `../../src/…`.
- **Vitest**. The default environment is Node. Tests that need a DOM (only `test/renderers/`)
  start with `// @vitest-environment jsdom`.
- Always test math against known values **and** properties
  (e.g. `M · M⁻¹ = I`, rotation preserves length, normals point outwards).
- Compare floats with `toBeCloseTo` or the `expectVec` helper, never with `toBe`.
- Every bug fix gets a test that fails without the fix.
- `npm run check` (which includes `npm test`) must be green before every merge
  into `develop`.
